# Eternal V4 — UI/UX Master Rule

STANDARD_VERSION: ETERNAL_V4_UIUX_1.0
SOURCE_PLUGIN: eternal-cursor-workflow v0.1.24
OWNER_DECISION_DATE: 2026-11-27
REPOSITORY: eternalsabloncup-star/eternal-produksi-v4

## Activation

Mandatory for:
- UI/UX task.
- Layout or visual task.
- Frontend implementation.
- Responsive or CSS change.
- Component, form, table or modal change.
- Frontend state/API changes affecting user behavior.
- Backend changes that materially affect UI state,
  actions, permissions or displayed information.

Backend-only work with no UI impact does not require
full browser visual QA.

Glob activation is not the only trigger.
Explicit task intent also activates this standard.

Before applicable implementation, read:

.cursor/skills/eternal-v4-design-system/SKILL.md
.cursor/skills/eternal-v4-layout-system/SKILL.md
.cursor/skills/eternal-v4-frontend-engineering/SKILL.md
.cursor/skills/eternal-v4-visual-qa/SKILL.md
.cursor/skills/eternal-v4-uiux-quality-gate/SKILL.md

Validate actual rule metadata syntax in Cursor.
Do not assume glob activation works without evidence.

## Authority and precedence

1. Owner-approved decisions and authorized scope.
2. Locked business rules, security, RBAC and data safety.
3. Eternal V4 engineering workflow.
4. ETERNAL_V4_UIUX_1.0 visual and FE standards.
5. eternal-fast-precision execution discipline.
6. antislop as complementary quality guidance.

Visual preferences must never override business gates,
security, authorization, data integrity or release gates.

The existing eternal-fast-precision skill references
the legacy repository. For this project, use the actual
V4 repository and V4 environment only.

Antislop must not replace Eternal's identity,
operational density or approved component behavior.

If a material conflict remains, HOLD and report it.

## Roles

Owner: Design and Business Authority.
ChatGPT: UI/UX Architect and Reviewer.
Cursor: Frontend Engineering Executor.

Cursor may suggest technical improvements but must not
make material design or business decisions independently.

## Workflow

Targeted read-only audit.
Approved design contract.
Implementation within approved scope.
Browser visual and functional QA.
Self-correction.
UI/UX Quality Gate.
Read-only production baseline smoke.
Owner preview approval.
Authorized Git finalization.
Exact HEAD CI.
Cross-PR Semantic Conflict Gate.
Final Merge Review.
Explicit Owner merge approval.
Separate Owner release approval.
Controlled deployment.
Postdeploy UI parity.

ONE PROMPT — ONE MILESTONE.

Do not fragment approved implementation into micro tasks.

## Synchronization

The ChatGPT plugin retains the architect rules and
shared standards. Repository skills are the executable
Cursor copy of the same shared standards.

Do not silently edit shared standards.
Any policy change requires Owner approval and
version synchronization between ChatGPT and Cursor.

If required skills cannot be read, do not fabricate
their contents. Report the blocker.
